second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What sport is David Hancock associated with?\", \"slot_hint\": \"sport\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 116, \"text\": \"Dave Hancock (footballer) David Jeffrey Hancock (24 July 1938 – 6 June 2007) was an English professional footballer.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d00\", \"start\": 117, \"end\": 257, \"text\": \"He was born in Exeter, Devon and played for all three of the county's professional football teams as well as for the National Team, England.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d00\", \"start\": 258, \"end\": 356, \"text\": \"Hancock began his career as a junior with Plymouth Argyle, turning professional in September 1955.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d00\", \"start\": 357, \"end\": 516, \"text\": \"He played twice in the league for Argyle during the 1956–57 season, but failed to make any further appearances and left to join Torquay United in January 1959.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d00\", \"start\": 517, \"end\": 600, \"text\": \"He made 177 league appearances for Torquay, scoring twelve goals, and played in the\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 98, \"text\": \"David Hancock (cricketer) David Arthur Hancock (born 28 March 1940) is a former English cricketer.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d01\", \"start\": 99, \"end\": 133, \"text\": \"Hancock was a left-handed batsman.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d01\", \"start\": 134, \"end\": 185, \"text\": \"He was born in Newcastle-under-Lyme, Staffordshire.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d01\", \"start\": 186, \"end\": 299, \"text\": \"Hancock made his debut for Staffordshire in the 1958 Minor Counties Championship against the Yorkshire Second XI.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d01\", \"start\": 300, \"end\": 430, \"text\": \"Hancock played Minor counties cricket for Staffordshire from 1958 to 1983, which included 204 Minor Counties Championship matches.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d01\", \"start\": 431, \"end\": 621, \"text\": \"In his entire Minor Counties Championship career for Staffordshire, he scored 9,303 runs at an average of 27.93, making 51 half centuries and 8 centuries, which included a high score of 148.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d01\", \"start\": 622, \"end\": 650, \"text\": \"He made his List A debut for\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 181, \"text\": \"retirement after serving one term in the Legislature for the Alberta Liberal Party left open the constituency of Edmonton-Whitemud, the riding once held by former Premier Don Getty.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d02\", \"start\": 182, \"end\": 354, \"text\": \"Hancock secured the PC nomination and squared off against Corky Meyer of the Liberals and Charan Khehra of the Alberta New Democratic Party in the 1997 provincial election.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d02\", \"start\": 355, \"end\": 647, \"text\": \"He won the constituency with 51 per cent of the vote, beating runner-up Meyer by 2,020 votes and was one of only two Progressive Conservatives elected in Edmonton's 19 constituencies (Julius Yankowsky, Edmonton-Beverly-Clareview, was the other.) Hancock was returned to the Legislature in the\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"David Hancock\", \"scope\": \"sport\", \"claim\": \"David Hancock is associated with football.\", \"answer\": \"football\", \"quote\": \"Dave Hancock (footballer) David Jeffrey Hancock (24 July 1938 – 6 June 2007) was an English professional footballer.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0301-40fbda82e379:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"David Hancock\", \"scope\": \"sport\", \"claim\": \"David Hancock is associated with cricket.\", \"answer\": \"cricket\", \"quote\": \"David Hancock (cricketer) David Arthur Hancock (born 28 March 1940) is a former English cricketer.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"football\", \"cricket\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"football\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"cricket\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C2\", \"answer\": \"politics\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}]}"
